          {
            "caution_id": "evidence-gap:b288a4186eb2cfc4d5c6a2f4",
            "description": "Missing-protein integration schema: Preserve the batch-dependent missingness and shared-gene assumptions; no blanket raw paired matrix requirement or imputation guarantee.",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "content_hash": "0f7637785c8c8230e6079af6b5ac6cb7770c7b1082cf5438ae7edcdb306d1ead",
                "end_offset": 44047,
                "evidence_span_id": "evidence-span:801f068a414588df49746e2f",
                "exact_text": "Here we adapted the training procedure from [65] to handle missing protein data. As any single batch may correspond to an experiment that used a different protein panel (or no proteins in the case of a scRNA-seq experiment), the missingness of protein features depends on the batch index sn. Further, suppose all batches share the same set of genes. Across all batches, there are T proteins. For cell n, we denote the observed protein expressions ynobs and the unobserved protein expressions ynmis. The log likelihood of the observed data decomposes as\n(11)logpv(x1:N,y1:Nobs,s1:N)=∑n=1Nlogpv(xn,ynobs|sn)",
                "locator": {
                  "kind": "section",
                  "value": "source-artifact:884e738e91cfb0cab46306828a98280f/xml:/article/body/sec[4]/sec[2]/sec[2]/p[1];text-sha256:3766e1d43421d5144d2a92c51830bb6ffc8e9e12f94c524c377faacb41a9aa1e:43442:44047"
                },
